abstract: >-
  Offline tools for biodiversity checklists, each a single HTML file that runs in a
  web browser with nothing installed and nothing uploaded. The Phylogenetic Checklist Viewer
  arranges a plant checklist in the order of current phylogenetic classifications (APG V for
  angiosperms, PPG I for ferns and lycophytes, Yang et al. 2022 for gymnosperms, BPG 2024 for
  bryophytes; 706 families), shows present and absent families and each family's share of
  the checklist and of world diversity, and compares checklists with three similarity
  indices. The Checklist Comparer compares checklists of any group of organisms using the
  ranks in the user's own columns, with Jaccard, Sørensen and Simpson indices, an incidence
  matrix, UPGMA clustering, a name check that flags look-alike spellings but does not validate names, and a species-area fit. The Checklist Cleaner applies one table of name corrections
  (synonyms, misspellings, deletions or a new rank) to any number of checklists at once and
  returns corrected copies with a report of every change. None of the tools validates
  species names.
keywords:
